{
  "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
  "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Isaacson, you said there were two facts. Aren't there three? Isn't it a fact that after the plea bargain the defendant in essence broke his side of the bargain by committing a crime while he was in jail?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, I used to teach contract law and I'll tell you that would have been a breach of contract. That would have been a breach on his part."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lars R. Isaacson (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ISAACSON: The government in this case drafted a plea agreement, and most plea agreements -- I've practiced in the Northern District of Texas quite often, and virtually every plea agreement has a provision in it that says if the defendant does some type of criminal activity, thus it will render it void. This plea agreement did not have that in it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What would counsel say about a case in which it's unclear whether there is a breach?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Isaacson",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we recognize that technical defects in a plea agreement may not always require automatic reversal. However, the government must always fulfill completely the promises they have made in the agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF LISA H. SCHERTLER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Schertler",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That would create incentives on the part of defendants to -- to withhold objections."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But in talking about the division of the circuits, do you think all breaches of -- of plea agreements should be governed by precisely the same standard? Or do you think there are varying facts in different cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can you say just for me, because I am changing a little bit here in light of that question, but what is it precisely that the government said it would do that it did not do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. SCHERTLER",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SCHERTLER: The -- paragraph 8 of the plea agreement indicates that the government --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: With respect, that is not what Olano says, is it? The -- the -- the basic Olano standard is a -- is a violation of substantial rights standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem that the Puckett panel had in\nthe third prong of 52(b) they focused on whether or not\nthere is prejudice at sentencing. That was the focus of\nthe Puckett panel. That is why they said 52(b) plain\nerror applied and was found in that case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The final point I would make is, the\nargument the government is making now about prejudice,\nit would make no difference at all if the defendant had\nobjected at the time. If there is no effect on\nsentencing, it would not pass muster under plain-error\nor the harmless error standards."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-9712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fc493ae52d06eac5ce09cf3080a5af174e24bd63e63f7a3801d3443136f71d75",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fc493ae52d06-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
